      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/enders_nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The post office opened on August 26, 1890, with William A. as its first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/enders_nebraska",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Enders received one of the first electrical grids in western Nebraska, powered by a dam on Frenchman Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
